  "overview_markdown": "OpenClaw is the original open-source personal AI assistant: a self-hosted Gateway that runs on your own hardware and connects to the chat platforms you already use — Discord, iMessage, Slack, Teams, Telegram, WhatsApp, and 20+ more — plus native apps for macOS, iOS, Android, Windows, and Linux. State, memory, and credentials stay on your devices, while model backends (Claude, Codex, local models) are swappable plugins, so the assistant is never tied to a single provider.\n\nArchitecturally, OpenClaw follows a 'trusted gateway, untrusted execution, deterministic policy' model: one Gateway process can serve as a personal assistant on a laptop or as a shared team deployment, with configuration as the only difference. Privacy is a stated priority — the only default phone-home is a daily version check, anonymous feature stats are opt-in, and telemetry can be fully disabled. The project is stewarded by the OpenClaw Foundation, an independent 501(c)(3), with no paid tier, hosted service, or token.\n\nRecent development shows a mature, high-velocity project: atomic updates with verified Gateway recovery, plugin hot reloading, worker startup and memory optimizations, local decision-model support via the TypeSafe plugin, and a public skill/plugin registry (ClawHub). Community sentiment is broadly positive but mixed on stability — Reddit threads praise its capability and ecosystem while some users report breakage after updates, reflecting the trade-off of its rapid release cadence and large feature surface.",
